WEBVTT

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:08.910
﻿We value your ability.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:14.120
﻿And we have the technology to
﻿increase that ability many times over.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.090
﻿The rest is up to you... Aila Jyrkiainen.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.030
﻿What do you want me to do?

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.230
﻿We want you to win at Gunpla Battle.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.470
﻿That's all we're asking from you.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.880
﻿Whatever. I'll do it.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.060
﻿The fighter of that white Gunpla.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.230
﻿Reiji...

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:05.100
﻿What's his reason for
﻿wanting to play Gunpla Battle?

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:11.910
﻿You'd lose against me anyway.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:05.110
﻿Yes!

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:07.370
﻿Yay!

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.650
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.230
﻿Thank you for your support, Mao.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.900
I wasn't just being nice.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.240
﻿I want to battle you two
﻿in a serious contest.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:13.410
﻿I want to make it clear
﻿whose Gunpla is better.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:17.340
﻿So I can't have you
﻿lose to some stranger first.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:23.350
- ﻿Yeah. When the time comes, then...
- ﻿Well give you no quarter.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:29.020
﻿Right back at you. See you later.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:35.130
﻿Aila.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:39.600
﻿Something wrong with the suit?

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.570
﻿No, there's no problem.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:50.340
﻿Reiji.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:54.080
﻿- Huh?
﻿- How's your injury?

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.520
﻿It's fine now.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.520
﻿I'm all in for the next battle.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.490
﻿That's good.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.420
﻿You're unbelievable.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:06.990
﻿Undefeated through the sixth period of
﻿the qualifiers, even with Reiji's injury.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:12.370
﻿- We were just lucky.
- ﻿It's our true strength!

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.240
Iori.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.740
﻿There are eight periods
﻿in the qualifiers, right?

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:21.110
﻿Yeah. Then the 16 players
﻿with the most points...

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:24.350
﻿will make it into the finals.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:29.950
﻿They've won all their battles,
﻿so they're in, right?

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:31.950
﻿No, not necessarily.

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:36.390
﻿There are other fighters who've
﻿also won all their battles.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:43.000
﻿First, there's Meijin Kawaguchi,
﻿participating as PPSE's special entry.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:46.470
﻿His Gunpla is the Kämpfer Amazing.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:51.810
﻿He's rumored to be the leading
﻿tournament contender. It's no bluff.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:57.540
Another potential champion
﻿is the main fighter of Team Nemesis,

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:00.950
﻿Aila Jyrkiainen, representing Finland.

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:04.850
﻿Her Gunpla is the Qubeley Papillon.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:09.160
﻿People still feel the shock
﻿from when she defeated...

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.330
﻿Carlos Kaiser, last year's champion.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:16.030
﻿Then there's the scientific prodigy
﻿who they call Samurai Boy,

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:19.970
﻿Nils Nielsen, representing America.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.840
﻿His Gunpla is the Sengoku Astray.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.240
﻿In this tournament,
﻿he's at the eye of the storm.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:29.610
﻿Also someone you both know well,

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:32.250
﻿Ricardo Fellini, representing Italy.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:37.120
﻿His Gunpla is the Wing Gundam Fenice.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:41.420
﻿And the builder who mastered
﻿the Gunpla Shingyo school,

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:45.060
﻿Mao Yasaka,
﻿representing Japan's 5th Block.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:49.100
﻿His Gunpla is the Gundam X Maoh.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:55.200
﻿Other than them, there's Morris,
﻿representing Australia.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.910
﻿Szpilman, representing Poland.
﻿Fox, representing Canada.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:02.980
﻿The Renato brothers,
﻿representing Argentina, and so on...

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:06.580
﻿A total of 12 players,
﻿including you two.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:11.520
﻿As well as 7 fighters who
﻿are 4 points behind,

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:14.760
﻿including Luang Dallara of Thailand,
﻿who you just defeated.

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:20.560
﻿You may be undefeated now,
﻿but depending on the seventh period,

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.730
﻿the ranking could still change.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:28.100
﻿Brace yourselves, you two.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.340
﻿Yes, sir!

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:36.180
﻿What!? What!!?? Whaaat!!!???

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.750
﻿Those kids haven't lost once!

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:41.120
﻿At this rate,
﻿they'll make it to the finals!

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:43.220
﻿I don't want that. I don't!

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:45.420
I ﻿don't!!!

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:51.360
﻿Why are you so concerned
﻿with the Sei Iori and Reiji team?

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.700
﻿B-Because...

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:57.200
﻿Th-They just bug me!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.300
﻿If they...

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.540
﻿If what?

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:06.470
﻿Anyway, make sure they
don't reach the final tournament!

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.310
﻿Yes, sir.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:13.110
﻿If you say so,
﻿I’ll call in that man.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.820
﻿A man who accepts any task
﻿and executes it perfectly,

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:22.320
﻿as long as the price is right.

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:26.760
﻿The one called Codename: C.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:33.100
<i>﻿Hello everyone!</i>

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:36.540
﻿I'm Kirara, the Gunpla idol!

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:37.670
﻿Kiraran!

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:43.240
﻿The World Tournament organizers
﻿have just announced...

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:47.050
﻿the details of the seventh period!

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.520
The seventh-period event will be...

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:53.390
﻿Thump thump! Thump thump!

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.420
﻿A Gunpla Race!

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:01.260
The course is indicated
﻿with lights like this,

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:04.360
and there are some gates along the way.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:08.400
Contestants must pass these gates
﻿and go around the course 3 times.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:11.780
﻿10 Gunpla will compete in each race,

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.270
﻿and there'll be 9 races in total.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:19.610
﻿The first in the race gets 4 points,
﻿and the others get no points.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:25.250
﻿To get through the qualifiers,
﻿this race is a must-win!

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:30.160
﻿Fighters may choose any Gunpla
﻿they like for this race.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:33.390
<i>﻿Not only support craft
﻿like Base Jabbers and Dodais,</i>

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:37.400
<i>﻿but even fighter planes and tanks
﻿are allowed in this race.</i>

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.800
<i>﻿And now for the key point!</i>

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.400
﻿Tell me, Kirara?

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:46.910
<i>﻿Use of firearms is permitted
﻿during the race!</i>

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:48.680
﻿Are you serious!?

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.650
<i>﻿It's up to the fighters to decide...</i>

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:56.080
<i>﻿whether to go for speed,
﻿or win by taking out the other Gunpla.</i>

00:09:56.550 --> 00:10:00.520
<i>﻿Check out the fighters'
choice of Gunpla and strategies!</i>

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.420
﻿- Guess that's that.
﻿- It's fine.

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:08.700
﻿I’ve got the Star Build Strike's
﻿three systems all set to go.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:12.270
﻿You should see the doctor
﻿before tomorrow's race.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:15.170
﻿I'm fine. I'm all healed.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.800
﻿Just go already!

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:40.560
﻿Please take care.

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.730
﻿It's healed for good.

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:46.300
﻿I can't wait until tomorrow!

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:47.200
﻿Reiji.

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:54.980
﻿How do you know my name?

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:57.440
﻿I saw it on TV.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.680
﻿You're playing in the
﻿Gunpla Battle tournament, right?

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:01.650
﻿Yeah.

00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:03.550
﻿You're rather childish.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:06.190
﻿How can you be
﻿so serious about a game?

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:09.160
﻿It's because it's just a game
﻿I can take it seriously.

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:12.660
﻿You should try it.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:14.860
﻿It's more fun than you think.

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:19.930
﻿H-Hey!

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:24.840
﻿It's not fun at all.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.440
﻿It's just painful.

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:34.780
﻿We've entered the final lap
﻿of the third race!

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:41.890
<i>﻿Watch how fast I am!</i>

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:43.520
<i>﻿Coming right through!</i>

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:49.760
﻿Are you watching me, my dear Kirara?

00:11:50.030 --> 00:11:54.370
<i>﻿And that was Mao Yasaka,
﻿the winner of the second race!</i>

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.570
﻿She's not even looking!

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:02.480
<i>﻿I was waiting for you to lap me, Fellini.</i>

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:05.780
﻿I'm already eliminated
﻿in the qualifiers

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:09.150
﻿But I'm not the type to just give up.

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:12.350
﻿I'll get in your way!

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.090
﻿See ya!

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:17.790
﻿I'll leave no traces!

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:22.360
﻿Finish!

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:26.300
<i>﻿The winner of the third race
﻿is Ricardo Fellini!</i>

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:35.510
﻿It's a souped-up version
﻿that depends on power output.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:37.940
<i>﻿I knew you'd be able to control it.</i>

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:41.520
﻿Naturally. I'm a Meijin!

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:47.390
<i>The winner of the fourth race
﻿is Meijin Kawaguchi!</i>

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:57.560
<i>﻿The winner of the fifth race
﻿is Aila Jyrkiainen!</i>

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:02.000
<i>﻿The winner of the sixth race
﻿is Luang Dallara!</i>

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:07.340
<i>﻿The winner of the seventh race
﻿is Nils Nielsen!</i>

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:13.350
﻿As I thought they're all good.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.480
﻿We can't lose against them.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.350
﻿Let's do this!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.190
﻿Yeah.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.620
﻿I'm sorry, China.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:26.960
﻿I overslept again.

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.600
﻿I guess my age is starting
﻿to get to me.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:32.470
﻿How old are you, Mr. Ral?

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:34.900
﻿Me? I'm 35.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:36.100
﻿Huh?

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:37.700
﻿What?

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:41.880
﻿N-Nothing. I think that's... wonderful.

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.820
﻿Mr. Ral, hurry!

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:49.550
﻿Yes.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.920
﻿China, go ahead without me.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.870
﻿What is he doing here?

00:14:18.310 --> 00:14:22.080
<i>﻿We'll now begin the ninth and final race.</i>

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:25.750
﻿I made it.

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:29.620
﻿Iori, good luck.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.480
﻿Stick to the plan, okay?

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.220
﻿Trust me, I got it!

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:04.690
Go!!!

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.530
- ﻿It's fast!
﻿- I don't think so.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:10.460
﻿Fire! Fire! Fire!

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:20.340
﻿Reiji, discharge!

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:21.640
﻿Yeah!

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:39.390
﻿Whoa, unbelievable speed!

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:40.930
﻿Can he control it?

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:46.300
﻿They're trying so hard.

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:50.670
﻿Yes! Just as we planned.

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:53.670
﻿With this lead,
﻿they won't be able to attack us.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:56.710
﻿Now, we just have to keep
﻿this distance and drive safely.

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:58.910
<i>﻿Leave it to me!</i>

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:04.890
﻿The Star Build Strike is
﻿at the top with a huge lead!

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:15.030
﻿Leading the first lap
﻿is the Star Build Strike!

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:34.280
﻿What!?

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:38.450
﻿The machine's being pulled!

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:42.390
﻿What's going on!?

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:46.760
﻿Th-That Gunpla is...!?

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:59.340
<i>﻿There's trouble in the ninth race!</i>

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:02.510
<i>﻿The Star Build Strike has fallen
﻿in a lake and isn't coming up.</i>

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:06.410
﻿- <i>What do you think happened?</i>
- ﻿<i>Um... I don't know.</i>

00:17:07.650 --> 00:17:09.950
﻿What do you mean, "I don't know"!?

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:14.020
﻿The other machines are
﻿passing it, one by one!

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:16.990
﻿Iori!

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.330
Good!

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:22.530
﻿Good! Good!
﻿They aren't coming up.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:26.870
﻿By now, their Gunpla should be...

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.940
﻿What is this!?

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:35.480
﻿Darn!

00:17:45.150 --> 00:17:47.550
T﻿his is bad! At this rate...

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:52.190
﻿Hey!

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:54.190
﻿What're you doing here?

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:56.860
﻿That's the Star Build Strike...

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:59.200
﻿It's supposed to be racing.

00:18:01.570 --> 00:18:03.700
﻿Are you interfering with the race!?

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:06.670
﻿I won't let you do that!

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.500
﻿No!

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.400
﻿Leave them alone.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.240
﻿Not only those two...

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:47.180
﻿But never get in the way
﻿of anyone...

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:49.750
﻿who takes Gunpla Battle seriously!

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:58.890
﻿Looks like this is it.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.760
﻿Why are you after them?

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:05.200
﻿Who asked you to do this?

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:13.010
﻿Sei! We ready yet?

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:15.410
﻿We're back on!

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:18.510
﻿Reiji, use the RG System
﻿with the arms only.

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:21.310
﻿Be careful not to overdo it,
﻿or it'll damage the machine!

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:22.680
﻿I know!

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:37.500
﻿What happened just now!?

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.340
﻿It's the Star Build Strike!

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:46.770
﻿Iori!

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:48.640
﻿It's back in the race!

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:50.340
﻿Yes!

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:54.580
﻿But the lost time has left it
﻿trailing far behind the leader!

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:56.150
﻿Will it catch up in time?

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:57.950
﻿Sei, how's the discharge?

00:19:58.120 --> 00:19:59.990
﻿Particles remaining, 28%.

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:02.420
﻿Only 56 seconds of full discharge left!

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:04.360
﻿That's enough!

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:14.370
﻿The Star Build Strike passes
the main stand at an incredible speed!

00:20:15.070 --> 00:20:18.300
﻿It's still trying for the lead,
﻿but can it catch up!?

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:23.340
﻿It's passed the FLAT to
﻿get out of last place!

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:27.180
﻿It's passed the Gabthley and Zudah, too!

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:31.780
﻿It's passed the G-Armor
﻿to take the sixth spot!

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:42.930
﻿It's passing the Moebius Zero
﻿and Gundam Maxter!

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:45.330
﻿It's an incredible comeback
﻿for the Star Build Strike!

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:48.200
﻿The Kyrios and Den'an Zon
﻿are right ahead!

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:53.470
The Star Build Strike has
﻿risen to second place!

00:20:53.970 --> 00:20:54.840
﻿10 more seconds!

00:20:55.740 --> 00:20:56.340
﻿I see it!

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:59.210
﻿The BuCUE Tank is in the home straight!

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:02.450
﻿The Star Build Strike is right behind!

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:05.650
﻿- Brother, behind us!
- ﻿I know.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:07.690
﻿Just a little further to the goal!

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:12.860
﻿Darn!

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:15.400
﻿Wow!

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:18.770
﻿The Star Build Strike has caught up
﻿to the BuCUE Tank!

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:20.330
<i>﻿Brother!</i>

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:23.300
﻿It's alright. Time's up.

00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:29.740
﻿Darn!

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:32.680
﻿Darn it!!!

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:34.580
﻿Finish!!!

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>﻿The winners of the ninth race are
﻿the Renato brothers.</i>

00:21:41.390 --> 00:21:44.320
﻿Sei and Reiji couldn't make it.

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:46.330
﻿The seventh period is now over.

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:49.700
﻿Sei and Reiji have fallen to
﻿17th place in the qualifiers.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.870
﻿They've hit a yellow light
on their way to the finals!

00:21:54.670 --> 00:21:55.770
﻿We lost.

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:59.870
﻿What was with that Gunpla...?

00:23:40.170 --> 00:23:41.470
﻿This is delicious.

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:44.880
﻿Today's wine tastes so good.

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:46.880
﻿It's truly the sweet taste of victory.

00:23:52.850 --> 00:23:54.820
﻿What!!!???

00:23:55.740 --> 00:23:57.770
﻿The battle where
﻿fighters can't compromise!

00:23:57.770 --> 00:24:00.510
﻿This is a genuine Gunpla Battle!

00:24:00.510 --> 00:24:02.410
Next episode, "Fighter's Radiance".

00:24:02.410 --> 00:24:04.410
What are the fighters after?
